  "article": {
    "hero": {
      "title": "🍹 Mobile Bar Name Generator",
      "tagline": "Names for a horsebox bar, prosecco van or mobile bartending business, from Tow & Tonic to Betty the Horsebox."
    },
    "intro": "Good mobile bar names are fun to say at a wedding and fit on the side of a horsebox: a pun (<em>Hitched & Poured Bar Co.</em>), a cute name for the van itself (<em>Daisy the Bar Cart</em>) or something classy (<em>The Gold Leaf Wedding Bar</em>). This **mobile bar name generator** gives you names for a horsebox bar, prosecco van, bar cart or mobile bartending service in eight styles, including ones built from your town or your own name.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Eight good mobile bar names",
        "content": "<p>All eight came from the generator:</p><ul><li><strong>Hitched & Poured Bar Co.</strong>: a wedding pun that tells planners what you do.</li><li><strong>Fizz in a Field</strong>: perfect for outdoor weddings and festivals.</li><li><strong>Daisy the Bar Cart</strong>: a name for the vehicle itself, which guests remember.</li><li><strong>The Dinky Prosecco Van</strong>: cute and clear for small parties.</li><li><strong>The Gold Leaf Wedding Bar</strong>: classy enough for a luxury wedding supplier list.</li><li><strong>Hatch & Shaker</strong>: modern, from the serving hatch and the cocktail shaker.</li><li><strong>Gin in a Horsebox</strong>: says exactly what you are.</li><li><strong>Clean Pour Bar & Events</strong>: a professional name for a bartending service.</li></ul>"
      },
      {
        "heading": "What makes a mobile bar name work",
        "content": "<p>Your name goes on quotes, supplier lists and the vehicle, so it has to work in all three:</p><ul><li><strong>Name the vehicle</strong> (horsebox, prosecco van, tuk tuk, bar cart) because that's what couples and planners search for.</li><li><strong>Give the van a name</strong>, like a pet. It makes the bar the star of the photos.</li><li><strong>Weddings or corporate?</strong> Romantic and fizzy names suit weddings; a plain surname name suits office parties and conferences.</li></ul><p>In England and Wales, selling alcohol at an event usually needs either the venue's premises licence or a Temporary Event Notice, and a personal licence helps. In the US, rules vary by state and many events use the caterer's or venue's licence, so check locally.</p>"
      },
      {
        "heading": "Check it's free before you print the sign",
        "content": "<p>Press <strong>Check</strong> next to any name, or paste it into the <a href=\"../business-name-checker.html\">Business Name Checker</a>, to see whether the domain and social handles are free. Then search the company register (Companies House in the UK, your state's business register in the US) and the trade mark register for your kind of business. Wedding suppliers trade on Instagram, so make sure the handle is free before you letter the horsebox.</p><p>This is general guidance, not legal advice. For the full process, read <a href=\"../guides/business-naming-best-practices.html\">Business Naming Best Practices</a>.</p>"
      },
      {
        "heading": "Tips for mobile bars",
